    "result_text": "All 285 tests pass, including the new `Cp19Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreation.java`:\n- Logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`.\n- Records the authenticated user (via `SecurityContextHolder`), the new owner's id, and the membership number.\n- Reads the owner from the pipeline via `@Val Owner`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, keeping the same `transaction` governance. Placing it after `save` ensures the owner's id has been assigned by the time the audit line is written.\n\nThe audit line produced during the test confirms the format:\n`AUDIT - Owner created by user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`\n\nBecause the step runs only after every validation/quota/save step succeeds (all earlier steps throw on failure, which short-circuits via escalation handlers), the log fires only on genuinely successful creations.",
